                <pb facs="0165" n="67" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg67"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5315a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-06-07T16:00:00-04:00">June 7, 1932—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>149. Department’s 127, May 17, 5 p.m. In view of the improved situation at
                    Shanghai, it has now been decided to send the 31st Infantry back to Manila by
                    the next Army transport which calls at Shanghai during the last week of June.
                    This decision should be kept confidential until announced from Washington.</p>
                <p>The Department is informing the British, French and Italian Governments of this
                    decision and you may likewise inform your British, French and Italian
                    colleagues.</p>
                <p>Please inform the Consul General at Shanghai and the Commander-in-Chief of the
                    essentials of the above.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
